@startuml

title Workflow instance and step states

hide empty description

state "the workflow instance machine" as wi {
    state "start" as i_start <<start>>
    state "pending" as i_pend
    state "in_progress" as i_prog
    state "completed" as i_done
    state "failed" as i_fail
    state "compensating" as i_comp
    state "compensated" as i_compd
}

state "the workflow step machine" as ws {
    state "start" as s_start <<start>>
    state "pending" as s_pend
    state "in_progress" as s_prog
    state "completed" as s_done
    state "completed_with_warnings" as s_warn
    state "failed" as s_fail
    state "compensated" as s_compd
}

i_start --> i_pend : initial_start
i_pend --> i_prog : initial_start
i_prog --> i_done : complete
i_prog --> i_fail : fail
i_prog --> i_comp : begin_compensation
i_comp --> i_compd : finish_compensation
i_comp --> i_fail : fail_during_compensation
i_fail --> i_prog : retry

s_start --> s_pend : initial_start
s_pend --> s_prog : initial_start
s_prog --> s_done : complete
s_prog --> s_warn : complete_with_warnings
s_prog --> s_fail : fail
s_fail --> s_compd : compensate
s_fail --> s_prog : retry

note right of i_pend
    A run waits in =pending= until
    =initial_start= puts it in =in_progress=.
end note

note right of i_comp
    A reader of a compensating run knows the run
    is undoing its completed steps, and that its
    next state is =compensated= or =failed=.
end note

note right of s_pend
    A step waits in =pending= until
    =initial_start= puts it in =in_progress=.
end note

note right of s_done
    =completed= is the state in which a step
    keeps its result for the steps after it.
end note

note bottom of s_fail
    =failed= carries the step's error and log.
    =retry= resumes the step from it, and
    =compensate= rolls it back.
end note

note bottom of i_fail
    =failed= carries the run's error and keeps
    every completed step. =retry= resumes the
    run from the step that failed.
end note

note bottom of i_done
    =completed=, =failed= and =compensated= are
    the terminal run states.
end note

legend bottom
    Rounded state: a state a run or a step may occupy.
    Arrow: a declared transition, labelled with the event that causes it.
    A run ends in =completed=, =failed= or =compensated=; a step ends in
    =completed=, =completed_with_warnings=, =failed= or =compensated=.
end legend

@enduml
